# Vulnerabilities and misconfigurations ignored, each with its reason and its
# re-audit date. Trivy's plain .trivyignore has no per-path scoping (only
# .trivyignore.yaml does, and scripts/security-scan.sh never passes
# --ignorefile, so only the default ".trivyignore", this file, is read): an
# ID listed here is silenced repository-wide, not just for the one file that
# earned the exception. Read the reason before reusing one of these ids for
# a DIFFERENT Dockerfile: a new suite harness needs its OWN non-root user,
# never a free ride on this entry.
#
# AVD-DS-0002 (HIGH, "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with
# non-root user"): bench/harness/benchrun.Dockerfile only. Its containers
# (runner-99/runner-97, gateway-99/gateway-97, bench/harness/compose.yaml)
# talk to the HOST docker daemon over /var/run/docker.sock, bind-mounted in.
# Measured live on this station (2026-09-26): the socket is owned root:root,
# mode 0660 (Docker Desktop's own VM); a Linux station's socket is root:docker
# instead, with a GID that is not the same number on every host. A non-root
# user baked into the image at build time cannot know either GID in advance,
# and there is no clean way to join it at build time: the alternatives are
# either bind-mounting the socket world-writable (worse than running the
# container as root, since it widens the hole to every process on the box,
# not just this one), or an entrypoint script that chmod/chgrp's the socket
# or re-execs into the right group at container start, which is exactly the
# kind of workaround this fix intentionally avoids (it would also mutate a
# HOST resource shared with the real Docker daemon, from inside a container,
# on every run). Every other Dockerfile under bench/harness/ got a real
# non-root USER instead (agent, aider, bfcl, lcb, livebench, longbench,
# ruler); this is the one exception, not a precedent.
# Re-audit: 2027-03-01, or sooner if Docker ships a portable way to join an
# arbitrary host GID from a Dockerfile without an entrypoint script.
AVD-DS-0002
